  "worked_solution": "The height (or altitude) corresponding to $\\overset{―}{KL}$ is a line segment that \n\n- runs from the opposite vertex $J$ to the line $\\overset{⟷}{KL},$ and\n\n- is perpendicular to $\\overset{⟷}{KL}.$\n\nTo draw the height, we proceed as follows:\n\n- Extend the line segment $\\overset{―}{KL}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14248996/assets/8fa817d73f39106248403b6690757a701b2bdaf6e1b189a46572201d36f64554.png)\n\n- Draw the perpendicular from $J$ to $\\overset{⟷}{KL}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14248996/assets/737e030ba35f922fc67ed421bec7c072e5d2b6b2d1fda11d2f081453b541d4a8.png)",
